msgid "Quarkus style and content guidelines"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Guidelines are provided to help you to contribute clear and consistent "
"content that is also sourced in the required diataxis structure and "
"composition of Quarkus documentation."
msgstr ""

msgid "AsciiDoc syntax"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus docs use AsciiDoc syntax.\n"
"The following links provide background on AsciiDoc syntax and general "
"conventions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://redhat-documentation.github.io/asciidoc-markup-conventions/[AsciiDoc "
"Mark-up Quick Reference for Documentation]"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://docs.asciidoctor.org/asciidoc/latest/[AsciiDoctor User Manual]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://docs.asciidoctor.org/asciidoc/latest/syntax-quick-reference/"
"[AsciiDoc Syntax Quick Reference]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Language and grammar"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Write clear, concise, and consistent technical information in US English.\n"
"Write for a global audience with localization, translation, inclusivity, and "
"diversity in mind.\n"
"Try to use the following grammar styles:"
msgstr ""

msgid "link:https://developers.google.com/style/tense?hl=en[Present tense]"
msgstr ""

msgid "link:https://developers.google.com/style/voice?hl=en[Active voice]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"link:https://developers.google.com/style/person?hl=en[Second person (you)]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"link:https://developers.google.com/style/tone?hl=en[A conversational tone]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"link:https://developers.google.com/style/pronouns?hl=en[Gender neutral "
"language]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sentence length"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Shorter sentences are much easier to read and translate. Try to use less "
"than 32 words per sentence."
msgstr ""

msgid "Website publication"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Content from this repository is published to the https://quarkus.io/guides/"
"[Quarkus.io website]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Documentation built from the main branch is published nightly (main-"
"SNAPSHOT)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Documentation for other branches is published at release time."
msgstr ""

msgid "Titles and headings"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Regardless of content type, ensure that the main title and any headings in "
"your document are:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Goal-oriented and use the language and keywords of the audience"
msgstr ""

msgid "Descriptive and avoid filler words"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Between 3-12 words and 50-80 characters per line to optimize findability in "
"search engines"
msgstr ""

msgid "In sentence case capitalization style"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your titles and headings must also follow the specific guidance for the "
"Quarkus content types, as outlined in the following table:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Title guidance for different Quarkus content types"
msgstr ""

msgid "Content type"
msgstr ""

msgid "Should ..."
msgstr ""

msgid "Good example"
msgstr ""

msgid "Bad example"
msgstr ""

msgid "Concept"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"* Start with a noun that names the concept or topic\n"
"* Never start with an active verb, for example, an action word like "
"configure, install, or start\n"
"* Finish the implied sentence: \"Understanding ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Start with a noun that names the concept or topic"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Never start with an active verb, for example, an action word like configure, "
"install, or start"
msgstr ""

msgid "Finish the implied sentence: \"Understanding ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Security and authentication mechanisms in Quarkus"
msgstr ""

msgid "Discovering Reactive SQL Clients In Quarkus"
msgstr ""

msgid "How-To Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"* Start with an active verb in the imperative verb form, for example, "
"\"Create a ...\" or \"Secure a ...\"\n"
"* Be action-oriented or task-oriented, rather than feature-oriented\n"
"* Finish the implied sentence: \"How to ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Start with an active verb in the imperative verb form, for example, \"Create "
"a ...\" or \"Secure a ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Be action-oriented or task-oriented, rather than feature-oriented"
msgstr ""

msgid "Finish the implied sentence: \"How to ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Secure your Quarkus application with WebAuthn authentication"
msgstr ""

msgid "Applying WebAuthn Authentication In Quarkus"
msgstr ""

msgid "Reference"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"* Use a noun phrase to concisely summarize the content of the document\n"
"* Not include the word 'reference'\n"
"* Finish the implied sentence: \"About ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Use a noun phrase to concisely summarize the content of the document"
msgstr ""

msgid "Not include the word 'reference'"
msgstr ""

msgid "Finish the implied sentence: \"About ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate Reactive API configuration properties"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reference guide for Configuring Hibernate Reactive API Configuration "
"Properties"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tutorial"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"* Start with an active verb in the imperative verb form, for example, "
"\"Create a ...\" or \"Secure a ...\"\n"
"* State what task the user will complete, with emphasis on the key topic or "
"demonstrated activity\n"
"* Be action-oriented or task-oriented, rather than feature-oriented\n"
"* Be led by the needs of the user in learning mode.\n"
"* Finish the implied sentence: \"In this tutorial, you will ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"State what task the user will complete, with emphasis on the key topic or "
"demonstrated activity"
msgstr ""

msgid "Be led by the needs of the user in learning mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Finish the implied sentence: \"In this tutorial, you will ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create a Quarkus application in JVM mode by using the quick start example"
msgstr ""

msgid "Creating an App"
msgstr ""

msgid "File conventions"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source locations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"AsciiDoc files are in the `src/main/asciidoc` directory within the `docs` "
"module of the link:{quarkus-base-url}/tree/main/docs[Quarkus GitHub "
"repository]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Configuration documentation is generated from JavaDoc comments in Java "
"source files."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Java, YAML, and other source files can also be referenced by AsciiDoc files."
msgstr ""

msgid "Output locations"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration references"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Configuration reference documentation is generated from Javadoc comments "
"discovered in MicroProfile Config source files.\n"
"These generated files are in `target/asciidoc/generated/config/` (from the "
"project root)."
msgstr ""

msgid "AsciiDoc output to HTML"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"AsciiDoc processing creates HTML files in `docs/target/generated-docs/`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Templates"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create new documentation files with the appropriate template for the content "
"type:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Concepts"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use `docs/src/main/asciidoc/_templates/template-concept.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "How-To Guides"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use `docs/src/main/asciidoc/_templates/template-howto.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use `docs/src/main/asciidoc/_templates/template-reference.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tutorials"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use `docs/src/main/asciidoc/_templates/template-tutorial.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "File names"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus documentation uses a flat hierarchy."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The bulk of the file name should be some representation of its title.\n"
"Use all lowercase letters, separate words with hyphens, and avoid symbols "
"and special characters."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prefix"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use a common prefix to group-related documents.\n"
"Documents related to writing and contributing to Quarkus docs share the `doc-"
"` prefix, for example."
msgstr ""

msgid "Suffix"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use a suffix that reflects the document type (optional):"
msgstr ""

msgid "`-concept.adoc` for concept documents"
msgstr ""

msgid "`-howto.adoc` for how-to guides"
msgstr ""

msgid "`-reference.adoc` for references"
msgstr ""

msgid "`-tutorial.adoc` for tutorials"
msgstr ""

msgid "Document structure"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use the Quarkus templates to ensure that your content is consistent with the "
"preferred Quarkus documentation structure and style."
msgstr ""

msgid "Document header"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each document should define a header for document-scoped attributes.\n"
"Minimally, each document should define an id and a title, include common "
"attributes (`_attributes.adoc`), and set the diataxis type."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use the filename as the ID for the document."
msgstr ""

msgid "Define the document title following guidance in <<titles-headings>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Include common document attributes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specify the diataxis type: `concept`, `howto`, `reference`, or `tutorial`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Other common document header attributes"
msgstr ""

msgid "`:extension-status: preview`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use this attribute to flag special types of content. Valid values: "
"`experimental`, `preview`, `stable` (not usually used), and `deprecated`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`:summary: <text>`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use the summary to provide a concise (26 words or less) description of the "
"document.\n"
"The value of this attribute is used in tiles or other descriptions on the "
"website and is not required in newer diataxis-styled docs, as outlined in "
"<<abstracts-preamble>>.\n"
"If not present, the first sentence of the abstract is automatically used to "
"generate the tile summary."
msgstr ""

msgid "Abstracts (preamble)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The first paragraph in the main body is treated as the abstract, also "
"referred to as the preamble.\n"
"Add a short description that helps your audience quickly find and understand "
"the purpose and intent of the page.\n"
"The first sentence of the abstract provides a summary and gets automatically "
"added to the tile on the link:https://quarkus.io/guides/[Quarkus guides "
"homepage]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Try to write the abstract by using the following guidelines:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*User oriented:* Contains terms and keywords that are familiar to users."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Concise:* Avoids self-referential expressions and filler words, for example:"
""
msgstr ""

msgid "\"This document..\""
msgstr ""

msgid "\"This tutorial...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "\"The following...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "*Brief:* Is no more than three sentences long."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ensure that the first sentence explains the value and some benefits of the "
"content in 26 words or less."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the first sentence is too long or cannot be simplified to fit on the "
"website tile, you can define a ``:summary:`` attribute in the document "
"header attributes to serve that purpose.\n"
"For more information, see <<doc-header-optional>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Semantic line breaks"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Text in paragraphs, lists, and tables should be broken into pieces that are "
"easier to review{semantic-line-breaks}.\n"
"Start a new line at the end of each sentence, and split sentences themselves "
"at natural breaks between clauses."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sections"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Section titles should be written in sentence case rather than title case."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Start your document with a title, which in AsciiDoc is defined as a `= Level "
"0` heading.\n"
"Where appropriate, divide your content into subsections, which in AsciiDoc "
"are defined as  `== Level 1` to `====== Level 5`.\n"
"Do not skip any levels."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Deep nesting (`====== Level 4`, `====== Level 5`)\n"
"should be avoided whenever possible.\n"
"If you end up with deeply nested sections, think about the following:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Is this information in the right place?\n"
"For example, if this is a reference, should some of this content be moved to "
"a concept doc or how-to guide instead?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Can the content be reorganized to make it simpler to consume?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See xref:doc-concept.adoc[Quarkus documentation content types] for more "
"information about content types and organization."
msgstr ""

msgid "Links"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In general, prefer link:https://docs.asciidoctor.org/asciidoc/latest/macros/"
"url-macro/[url macros] to bare or automatic links.\n"
"Provide human-readable text for the link, especially if it is included in "
"the middle of other text."
msgstr ""

msgid "A URL Macro link with attributes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The URL macro also supports link:https://docs.asciidoctor.org/asciidoc/"
"latest/macros/link-macro-ref/[additional attributes] that may be relevant, "
"like opening a link in a different window."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The above source produces this link:https://docs.asciidoctor.org/asciidoc/"
"latest/syntax-quick-reference/[AsciiDoc Syntax Quick Reference,window="
"_blank,opts=nofollow]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cross-references"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus documentation is built from source in a few different environments."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cross-reference source attributes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We use attributes in our cross-references to ensure our docs can be built "
"across these environments."
msgstr ""

msgid "Attribute"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{code-examples}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative path to directory containing collected example source files"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{doc-examples}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative path to source examples for documentation guides"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{generated-dir}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative path to generated configuration `*.adoc` files"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{imagesdir}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative path to directory containing images"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{includes}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative path to directory containing partial/reusable content"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When cross-referencing content, always use the inter-document `xref:` syntax "
"and supply a human-readable label to your link."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The cross-reference starts with `xref:`, and provides a readable description:"
" `[Quarkus Documentation concepts]`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Anchors for in-file and cross-file navigation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To create an anchored ID, use lower-case characters, separate each word with "
"`-`, and enclose the ID in `[[]]` as in the example below."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To call an anchor created in the same file, insert the anchored ID in a "
"`<<>>` xref macro."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To create an anchor with a custom URL caption example, specify the anchored "
"ID and desired name separated by `,` without white space."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To call an anchored ID from a different file, use the full file name and "
"anchored ID separated by `#`,\n"
"and specify the human-readable URL caption."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To refer to another file, use the xref macro with the full file name syntax "
"and always specify the human-readable URL caption."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more details about anchored IDs, see the xref:doc-contribute-docs-howto."
"adoc#anchors-howto[Cross-reference in-file and cross-file content by using "
"anchors] section of the \"Contribute to Quarkus documentation\" guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cross-reference phrasing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For consistency and context clarity, use the following guidelines for "
"constructing your cross-reference phrases:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Provide a direct hyperlink to the section, using the `xref` guidance in the "
"previous section."
msgstr ""

msgid "Specify the full title of the section and use sentence case."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add the definite article “the” before the section title and specify "
"“section” directly after the title."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add the definite article “the” and “Quarkus” before the title of the guide, "
"unless the word “Quarkus\" is already in the title."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Insert the title of the guide between double quotations and specify “guide” "
"directly after the title."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the context is needed, lead with the phrase:"
msgstr ""

msgid "\"For more information about ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Correct and incorrect cross-reference phrases"
msgstr ""

msgid "Correct"
msgstr ""

msgid "Incorrect"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the xref:validation.adoc#configuring-the-"
"validatorfactory[Configuring the ValidatorFactory] section of the Quarkus "
"\"Validation with Hibernate Validator\" guide."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the 'Configuring the ValidatorFactory' section of "
"the xref:validation.adoc[VALIDATION WITH HIBERNATE VALIDATOR guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the xref:cache.adoc#generating-a-cache-key-with-"
"cachekeygenerator[Generating a cache key with CacheKeyGenerator] section of "
"the Quarkus \"Application Data Caching\" guide."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see xref:cache.adoc#generating-a-cache-key-with-"
"cachekeygenerator[Generating a cache key with CacheKeyGenerator]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the xref:security-openid-connect-web-"
"authentication/.adoc#proof-of-key-for-code-exchange-pkce[PKCE-related "
"section] of the Quarkus \"OpenID Connect (OIDC) Authorization Code Flow "
"Mechanism\" guide."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see xref:security-openid-connect-web-authentication."
"adoc#proof-of-key-for-code-exchange-pkce[OpenID Connect (OIDC) Authorization "
"Code Flow Mechanism]."
msgstr ""

